Sun Nov  1 20:56:06 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- New package openidea 0.1.33: an IntelliJ IDEA-style IDE with a
  Rust core, built as a Tauri desktop app on the system WebKitGTK.
  * The frontend is built offline with the system Node.js from
    vendored npm tarballs; the rolldown and lightningcss bindings
    vite needs are built from source.
  * Prebuilt jars and wasm modules are removed from the sources.
  * Pass -fno-strict-aliasing to the vendored tree-sitter grammars,
    avoiding the heap corruption of their old array.h on aarch64
    (gh#tree-sitter/tree-sitter-haskell#144).
  * openidea-server subpackage: the remote development server,
    which the IDE uploads to Linux hosts of the same architecture;
    they need libsqlite3 and a glibc at least as new as
    Tumbleweed's.
- Add openidea-no-self-update.patch: disable the in-app updater,
  updates come from the distribution.
- Add openidea-no-server-download.patch: do not download upstream's
  prebuilt openidea-server for remote development hosts.
- Add openidea-no-prebuilt-jars.patch: drop the embedded prebuilt
  JDT LS extensions and patched Lombok agent; jdtls takes Lombok
  from the project's Maven or Gradle cache or a -javaagent option.
- Add openidea-npm-build-deps.patch: vendor only the npm packages
  the build and the frontend tests use.
- Add openidea-rlib-only.patch: skip the mobile staticlib and
  cdylib library types, which cost two extra LTO passes.
- Add openidea-no-tool-installs.patch: do not download or install
  language servers, debuggers and formatters; name the openSUSE
  package to install instead.
- Add openidea-no-jdk-downloads.patch: do not download JDKs or a
  Java runtime for jdtls, and find the JDKs in /usr/lib64/jvm.
- Add openidea-no-agent-installs.patch: do not fetch the ACP
  Registry or install agents from it, and run the Claude Code and
  Codex ACP adapters from PATH instead of fetching them with npx.
- Add openidea-no-coverage-installs.patch: do not offer to install
  coverage and profiling tools (cargo-llvm-cov, c8, the vitest
  coverage provider, coverage.py, py-spy) from Run with Coverage
  and Profile.

